  ($q$cs-212$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 1, $q$Text 1: Entomologist A argues that firefly populations are declining mainly because of increased artificial light at night, which disrupts the flashing signals fireflies use to find mates.

