  ($q$cs-216$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Labor economist A argues that gig work expands economic opportunity by letting workers set flexible schedules unavailable in traditional jobs.

