  ($q$cs-219$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Urban historian A argues that a neighborhood's rapid gentrification was driven primarily by an influx of artists and small galleries that made the area culturally fashionable.

