  ($q$cs-222$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Neuroscientist A argues that short daytime naps are sufficient to consolidate newly learned information, citing memory tests showing improved recall after a thirty-minute nap.

