  ($q$cs-225$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The locksmith's work was impressively ______, able to open the antique safe without leaving a single scratch on its ornate surface.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["precise","destructive","slow","loud"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Opening a safe 'without leaving a single scratch' demonstrates precise work, the opposite of destructive.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-226$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The typeface designer's latest font was praised as ______, remaining easy to read even when shrunk to the smallest size on a phone screen.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["legible","ornate","illegible","decorative"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$A font that stays 'easy to read even when shrunk' is legible; the sentence rules out illegible or purely decorative.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-227$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The crossword constructor's puzzles grew ______ over the years, requiring solvers to know far more obscure trivia than her early, simpler grids had.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["demanding","forgiving","predictable","shorter"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Requiring 'far more obscure trivia' than earlier, simpler grids describes puzzles that became more demanding, not forgiving.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-228$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The stunt coordinator's plan for the car chase was ______, with every vehicle's path and speed calculated down to the second before filming began.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["meticulous","improvised","reckless","secretive"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Calculating every path and speed 'down to the second' before filming describes a meticulous plan, the opposite of improvised.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-229$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The soap maker's latest batch was ______, blending lavender, citrus, and cedar into a scent no single ingredient could achieve alone.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["layered","plain","bitter","faint"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Blending three scents into one effect 'no single ingredient could achieve alone' describes a layered scent, not a plain one.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-230$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The submarine captain's orders were ______, leaving no doubt among the crew about exactly what each person was expected to do.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["unambiguous","cryptic","optional","delayed"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Orders that leave 'no doubt' about what each person should do are unambiguous, the opposite of cryptic.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-231$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The auctioneer's pace was famously ______, rattling off bids so quickly that newcomers often missed their chance to raise a paddle.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["rapid","sluggish","hesitant","monotone"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Rattling off bids so quickly that newcomers miss their chance describes a rapid pace, not a sluggish or hesitant one.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-232$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$An article on the bicycle begins by describing the awkward, dangerously tall penny-farthing of the 1870s, then explains how the invention of the chain-driven 'safety bicycle' made cycling accessible to far more riders, including many women.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It moves from an early, flawed design to a later innovation that broadened who could use it.","It presents two rival theories about who invented the bicycle.","It argues that the penny-farthing was safer than later bicycle designs.","It compares bicycles to an unrelated form of transportation throughout."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The text moves from the flawed, dangerous penny-farthing to the safety bicycle that broadened access, matching the correct answer exactly.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-233$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$A history of surgery opens with an account of patients held down and given nothing but alcohol before an operation, then describes how the introduction of ether anesthesia transformed surgical practice almost overnight.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It shows how a specific innovation resolved the painful problem described in the first sentence.","It contradicts the account given in the first sentence.","It introduces an entirely unrelated medical procedure.","It argues that ether anesthesia was more dangerous than earlier methods."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence directly addresses the pain described in the first sentence by introducing the innovation that resolved it.$q$, null),
