  ($q$cs-239$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 1, $q$Text 1: Biologist A argues that birds sing at dawn primarily to defend territory, noting that males sing most intensely near the boundaries of their claimed area.

