  ($q$cs-255$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$Many assume that streaming made vinyl records a relic of the past. In fact, vinyl sales have risen for sixteen consecutive years, with some pressing plants now booked more than a year in advance.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?$q$, $q$["To complicate a popular assumption about vinyl records' relevance in the streaming era","To argue that streaming services should be banned","To describe the mechanical process of pressing a vinyl record","To praise a specific pressing plant for its efficiency"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The text states a common assumption and then complicates it with sales data ('in fact...'), matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-256$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An article on octopus camouflage opens by describing an octopus vanishing against a coral reef within a second, then explains that specialized skin cells called chromatophores allow the animal to change color almost instantly.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It explains the biological mechanism behind the behavior described in the first sentence.","It contradicts the claim made in the first sentence.","It introduces an unrelated marine animal's camouflage ability.","It argues that octopus camouflage is slower than commonly believed."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence identifies chromatophores as the mechanism that produces the rapid color change described in the first sentence.$q$, null),
