  ($q$cs-258$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A conservator's report opens with a photograph of a Roman floor mosaic missing nearly a third of its tiles, then details the painstaking process of sourcing matching stone to fill the gaps without altering the original design.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?$q$, $q$["To document how a damaged artifact was restored while preserving its original appearance","To argue that damaged mosaics should never be restored","To compare the mosaic to an unrelated artwork from a different era","To criticize the original artisans who created the mosaic"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The report moves from showing the damage to detailing a restoration that preserved the original design, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-259$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$Early wind turbine blades were short and flat, generating only modest amounts of power. Engineers later discovered that longer, subtly twisted blades captured far more energy from the same wind speed, a design now standard across the industry.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It contrasts an early, limited design with a later improvement that became the industry standard.","It presents two competing theories about wind speed measurement.","It argues that short blades remain superior to long ones.","It compares wind turbines to an unrelated renewable energy source."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The text contrasts the early short, flat blades with the later twisted design that became standard, matching the correct answer exactly.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-260$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A retrospective on a famous war photograph opens by celebrating the image's role in shifting public opinion, then spends its final section examining persistent questions about whether the scene had been partly staged for the camera.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the final section in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It complicates the earlier celebration by raising doubts about the photograph's authenticity.","It confirms without question that the photograph was entirely genuine.","It shifts focus entirely away from the photograph to an unrelated conflict.","It proves that staged photographs never influence public opinion."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$After celebrating the photograph, the final section raises doubts about its authenticity, complicating rather than confirming the earlier praise.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-261$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay on the skyscraper opens by noting that buildings taller than a few stories were impractical when every floor had to be reached by stairs, then explains how the invention of a safety brake that could stop an elevator from falling made tall buildings suddenly feasible.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It identifies the specific innovation that resolved the limitation described in the first sentence.","It contradicts the limitation described in the first sentence.","It introduces a completely unrelated architectural feature.","It argues that tall buildings were common before elevators existed."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence names the safety brake as the innovation that overcame the stair-climbing limitation described in the first sentence.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-262$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay on opera begins by describing audiences politely applauding performances in languages they could not understand, then explains how the introduction of projected supertitles let listeners follow the plot line by line for the first time.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?$q$, $q$["To show how a specific innovation changed audiences' ability to understand opera performances","To argue that opera should always be performed in the audience's native language","To criticize audiences for applauding performances they did not understand","To provide a technical history of stage lighting equipment"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The essay moves from describing audiences' confusion to explaining how supertitles resolved it, matching the correct answer's description of the purpose.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-263$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Economist A argues that a major cryptocurrency functions as an effective hedge against inflation, pointing to its fixed supply that cannot be increased by central banks.

