  ($q$cs-270$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The cartoonist's political strip grew increasingly ______, using a single panel to compress arguments that opinion columnists needed several paragraphs to make.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["economical","verbose","redundant","terse"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Compressing a full argument into one panel is not just brevity but skillful efficiency, which 'economical' conveys; 'terse' describes curt brevity that doesn't necessarily capture successfully compressed meaning — a terse panel could just as easily be cryptic or incomplete.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-271$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The upholsterer's restoration of the antique chair was ______, matching the original fabric's pattern so precisely that the repair was invisible to anyone who hadn't seen the chair before.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["seamless","conspicuous","skillful","mismatched"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The key detail is that the repair was 'invisible,' not merely well executed — 'seamless' captures undetectability specifically, while 'skillful' describes expert craftsmanship that could still be visible as a repair.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-272$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The kite maker's designs were ______, holding steady in gusts that sent every other kite at the festival spiraling to the ground.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["resilient","flimsy","erratic","durable"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The clue is withstanding sudden gusts in the moment, which 'resilient' captures as the capacity to flex and recover under stress; 'durable' instead describes lasting through long-term wear, not necessarily handling a sudden gust better than other kites.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-273$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The bonsai gardener's pruning was ______, removing growth so gradually over decades that the tree's miniature form never looked abruptly altered.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["incremental","drastic","careless","deliberate"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The clue is the slow accumulation of small changes over decades, which 'incremental' names precisely; 'deliberate' only means intentional and wouldn't rule out an intentional but drastic, one-time cut.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-274$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The radio host's interview style was ______, letting long silences sit unfilled so guests felt compelled to elaborate rather than give rehearsed answers.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["deliberate","rushed","scripted","patient"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The passage describes an intentional strategy — letting silences sit to draw out guests — which 'deliberate' names as a calculated technique; 'patient' describes a personal temperament and doesn't by itself capture that the silences were a deliberate interviewing tactic.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-275$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The blacksmith's technique was ______, reheating and reworking the same blade a dozen times until the metal's internal structure was uniform throughout.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["painstaking","hasty","slapdash","thorough"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Reworking the same blade 'a dozen times' emphasizes repeated, effortful care, which 'painstaking' captures; 'thorough' would describe comprehensive attention but doesn't necessarily imply the repetitive labor that produced the uniform structure.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-276$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An economic history essay opens with a detailed account of two neighboring villages exchanging surplus grain for woven cloth, then argues that such direct barter arrangements, far from being primitive, required dense social trust networks more intricate than many early currency systems that replaced them.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?$q$, $q$["To complicate the assumption that barter was a simpler precursor to currency","To argue that currency was never actually adopted by most societies","To argue that barter required less social trust than the currency systems that replaced it","To criticize the villages for refusing to adopt currency"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The essay explicitly argues that barter required trust networks 'more intricate' than later currency systems, not less — complicating, rather than reversing, the simpler-precursor assumption.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-277$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A profile of a basket weaver opens with her hands moving through a pattern passed down from her grandmother, then traces how the same technique, once common throughout the region, nearly disappeared within a single generation before a recent revival among young craftspeople.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It moves from a personal illustration of a tradition to its near-loss to its recent resurgence.","It presents two competing weaving techniques and argues for one over the other.","It opens with the tradition's revival and ends with its origin.","It credits the technique's revival mainly to her grandmother's generation rather than recent young craftspeople."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The profile moves in sequence from a personal illustration of the tradition, to its near-disappearance, to its recent revival among young craftspeople, not her grandmother's generation, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-278$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A city planning report opens by noting that the city tore out its streetcar tracks in the 1950s to make room for automobiles, then details a current proposal to lay new light-rail lines along nearly the same routes those streetcars once followed.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It highlights an ironic return to a transportation approach the city had earlier abandoned.","It confirms that automobiles remain the city's preferred mode of transportation.","It proposes rerouting the light-rail lines away from the streetcars' original paths.","It proves that the original streetcar removal was a mistake with no further explanation needed."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Proposing light-rail lines along 'nearly the same routes' the city once tore up for cars highlights a return to the earlier approach, not a rerouting away from it, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-279$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A history of global communication opens with a dramatic account of the first transatlantic telegraph cable failing within weeks of its 1858 completion, then describes the engineering refinements that finally produced a cable reliable enough to operate for decades.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It contrasts an early failure with a later engineering success that achieved lasting reliability.","It argues that transatlantic communication was impossible before satellites.","It argues that the 1858 cable's failure proved the entire cable project was misguided.","It opens with the successful cable and ends with its failure."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The text moves from the cable's early failure to the later refinements that achieved decades of reliable operation, not to a conclusion that the project itself was misguided, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-280$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay on home heating opens by describing residents waking repeatedly through the night to manually stoke a furnace, then explains how the invention of a thermostat that automatically regulated temperature freed households from that constant attention.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It identifies the specific invention that resolved the burdensome task described in the first sentence.","It disputes that residents ever needed to stoke furnaces manually.","It credits the furnace itself, rather than the thermostat, with ending the need for manual stoking.","It argues that automatic temperature regulation was less convenient than manual stoking."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence specifically names the thermostat, not the furnace itself, as the invention that freed residents from the nightly stoking described in the first sentence.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-281$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Paleoanthropologist A argues that a major leap in early stone tool sophistication was driven by a shift to a colder climate that forced populations to develop better hunting technology to survive.

Text 2: Paleoanthropologist B argues that the same leap was driven by larger social groups forming around that time, which allowed toolmaking knowledge to spread and improve through social learning regardless of climate.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes a key difference between the two paleoanthropologists' views?$q$, $q$["Paleoanthropologist A emphasizes environmental pressure, while Paleoanthropologist B emphasizes social transmission of knowledge.","Both paleoanthropologists agree that climate had no role in the tool innovation.","Paleoanthropologist B attributes the innovation entirely to colder temperatures.","Paleoanthropologist A argues that larger social groups caused the innovation."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Paleoanthropologist A points to climate-driven necessity, while Paleoanthropologist B points to social-group knowledge transfer — the contrast in the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-282$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Urban ecologist A argues that installing green roofs across a city meaningfully reduces summer building temperatures, citing rooftop sensors that recorded notably cooler surface temperatures than on bare roofs.

Text 2: Urban ecologist B argues that green roofs are not a cost-effective cooling strategy for most buildings, noting that the installation and irrigation costs over a roof's lifetime exceed the value of the modest energy savings achieved.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes how Urban ecologist B would likely respond to Urban ecologist A's claim?$q$, $q$["B would acknowledge the cooling effect but argue it does not justify the long-term costs involved.","B would deny that green roofs have any measurable cooling effect at all.","B would agree that green roofs are the most cost-effective cooling strategy available.","B would claim that rooftop sensors cannot accurately measure temperature."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Ecologist B's argument concerns cost-effectiveness, not whether cooling occurs, so B would accept the cooling effect while disputing its economic value.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-283$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Sports physiologist A argues that the sharp fatigue many marathoners feel around mile twenty is caused primarily by the depletion of stored glycogen in the muscles, forcing the body to rely on a less efficient fuel source.

Text 2: Sports physiologist B argues that the same fatigue is primarily psychological, pointing to runners who, when told they had less distance left than they actually did, maintained their pace well past where the 'wall' typically occurs.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes a key difference between the two physiologists' explanations?$q$, $q$["Physiologist A points to a physical fuel limitation, while Physiologist B points to a psychological factor.","Both physiologists agree that glycogen depletion is irrelevant to marathon fatigue.","Physiologist B attributes the fatigue entirely to muscle fuel depletion.","Physiologist A argues that deception about distance eliminates fatigue."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Physiologist A attributes the 'wall' to glycogen depletion, while Physiologist B attributes it to psychological expectation — the contrast in the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-284$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Epidemiologist A argues that a disease outbreak in a coastal town spread primarily through a contaminated water supply, citing case clusters concentrated among households served by a single well.

Text 2: Epidemiologist B argues that the outbreak spread primarily through airborne transmission at a crowded indoor market, citing cases among visitors who never drank water from the implicated well.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes a key difference between the two epidemiologists' explanations for the outbreak?$q$, $q$["Epidemiologist A points to a contaminated water source, while Epidemiologist B points to airborne spread at a public venue.","Both epidemiologists agree the outbreak had no connection to the well.","Epidemiologist B attributes the outbreak entirely to the contaminated well.","Epidemiologist A argues that the market was the source of the outbreak."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Epidemiologist A points to the contaminated well, while Epidemiologist B points to airborne spread among market visitors who avoided that well — the contrast in the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-285$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The new app's interface was praised as ______: first-time users navigated every major feature without ever consulting the help guide.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["intuitive","convoluted","outdated","expensive"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Users who navigated the app without consulting help describe an intuitive interface, not a convoluted or outdated one.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-286$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$Forecasters described the storm's path as ______, since it changed direction four times in a single afternoon despite constant satellite tracking.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["erratic","predictable","gentle","delayed"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Changing direction four times in one afternoon describes an erratic path, not a predictable or gentle one.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-287$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The restorer's cleaning of the fresco was ______, removing centuries of grime one square centimeter at a time with a fine brush.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["meticulous","careless","hurried","random"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Removing grime 'one square centimeter at a time' describes a meticulous process, not a careless or hurried one.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-288$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$Facing a mutiny among her own advisors, the queen acted ______, dismissing three ministers within a single day rather than deliberating for weeks.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["decisively","hesitantly","apologetically","indifferently"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Dismissing three ministers in a single day, rather than deliberating, describes decisive action, not hesitation.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-289$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The experiment's result was ______: particles separated by vast distances appeared to influence each other instantaneously, defying classical expectations.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["counterintuitive","predictable","trivial","paradoxical"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$'Defying classical expectations' describes a result that confounds intuition, which 'counterintuitive' names; 'paradoxical' implies an internal logical contradiction, a stronger claim than simply being surprising or hard to anticipate.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-290$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$Even after two season-ending injuries, the sprinter remained ______, returning to full training within months each time.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["relentless","resigned","cautious","indifferent"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Returning to full training quickly after repeated injuries describes a relentless athlete, not a resigned or cautious one.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-291$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$Because respondents interpreted the survey question in several different ways, the results were ultimately ______ rather than offering any clear answer.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["inconclusive","definitive","alarming","unanimous"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Results that fail to offer 'any clear answer' because of varied interpretations are inconclusive, not definitive or unanimous.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-292$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$Despite years of camera traps set throughout the forest, the rare cat remained ______, with researchers capturing only a handful of blurry images.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["elusive","abundant","docile","conspicuous"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Years of effort yielding only 'a handful of blurry images' describes an elusive animal, not an abundant or conspicuous one.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-293$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$Engineers admitted the algorithm's decision-making process was ______, producing results that even its own designers struggled to explain.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["opaque","transparent","simple","complex"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The clue is that designers 'struggled to explain' the results — a failure of understanding, which 'opaque' captures figuratively; 'complex' only means having many parts, and a complex system can still be fully explainable, unlike one that is opaque.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-294$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The peace agreement proved ______, collapsing within a year as both sides resumed the hostilities it was meant to end.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["tenuous","durable","celebrated","permanent"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$An agreement that 'collapsed within a year' was fragile, or tenuous, not durable or permanent.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-295$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$Audiences found the cellist's final note strangely ______, a single sustained tone that lingered in the concert hall long after the piece ended.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["haunting","cheerful","forgettable","abrupt"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$A tone that 'lingered long after the piece ended' is memorable and evocative, which 'haunting' captures, not 'forgettable' or 'abrupt.'$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-296$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$Unlike the sudden collapse of the neighboring cliff, the shoreline's erosion here has been ______, retreating only a few centimeters each year.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["gradual","sudden","reversible","negligible"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Retreating 'only a few centimeters each year,' in contrast to a sudden collapse, describes gradual erosion.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-297$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$Currency traders described the market as ______ that week, with prices swinging several percentage points within hours on rumors alone.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["volatile","stable","sluggish","erratic"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The clue specifies swings of 'several percentage points within hours' — a matter of magnitude and speed, which 'volatile' names precisely; 'erratic' only implies a lack of consistent pattern and doesn't specifically convey swings of that size and speed.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-298$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$During her thirties alone, the novelist was remarkably ______, publishing eleven books while also writing for two magazines.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["prolific","idle","secretive","reluctant"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Publishing eleven books while also writing for two magazines describes a prolific output, not an idle or reluctant one.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-299$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The drought-resistant shrub proved ______, flowering again within weeks of the first rainfall after an entire dry summer.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["resilient","delicate","dormant","diseased"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Flowering again quickly after a dry summer shows the shrub recovers well, which 'resilient' captures, not 'delicate' or 'diseased.'$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-300$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$Many assume that Mars's thin atmosphere could never have supported liquid water. Yet mineral deposits found by a rover closely resemble those left by evaporating lakes on Earth, suggesting ancient water once existed there.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It presents evidence that complicates the assumption stated in the first sentence.","It restates the assumption from the first sentence in different words.","It introduces an unrelated topic about Martian geology.","It summarizes the passage's conclusion before any evidence is given."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The mineral deposits described in the second sentence suggest ancient water, directly complicating the assumption introduced in the first sentence.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-301$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A report on a city's bike-lane program opens by citing a sharp rise in cyclist injuries during its first year, then devotes its remaining pages to data showing injuries fell well below pre-program levels once drivers adjusted to the new lanes.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?$q$, $q$["To complicate an alarming early statistic with the fuller trend that followed","To argue that bike lanes should never be installed in cities","To provide a technical manual for painting bike lanes","To praise the official who proposed the program"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The report opens with a troubling early statistic, then shows how the fuller data tell a different story, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-302$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$An article on dye-making opens with a description of indigo leaves being crushed into paste, then explains the chemical oxidation process that turns the paste a deep blue, and closes by noting how some artisans still prefer this slow method today.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It moves from a vivid process description to scientific explanation to a reflection on tradition.","It presents two rival theories of dye chemistry and refutes one of them.","It opens with a conclusion and works backward to the evidence supporting it.","It compares indigo dyeing to an unrelated craft throughout the article."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The article's stated progression — process, then chemistry, then a closing reflection on tradition — matches the correct answer exactly.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-303$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A linguistics essay first praises a region's dialect for preserving archaic vocabulary lost elsewhere, then spends its remaining paragraphs noting how the same isolation that preserved the dialect is now causing it to disappear as young speakers migrate elsewhere.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the essay's final paragraphs?$q$, $q$["They complicate the initial praise by introducing an unintended consequence of the same isolation.","They repeat the praise from the opening without adding anything new.","They attribute the dialect's decline to outside interference rather than the isolation that preserved it.","They prove that the dialect was never actually endangered."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$After praising the dialect's preservation, the final paragraphs show the very same isolation now causing its disappearance, not some outside interference, complicating rather than repeating the earlier praise.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-304$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$The middle section of an article on street vendors presents interviews with five vendors describing how informal lending networks let them restock inventory daily; the conclusion then recommends formal microloan programs modeled on those networks.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the middle section of the article?$q$, $q$["To provide concrete examples that support the recommendation offered later","To contradict the claims made in the article's introduction","To define technical terms related to microfinance","To criticize the vendors interviewed as unreliable"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Vendor interviews presented before the conclusion's recommendation function as supporting evidence for that recommendation, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-305$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$A chemistry chapter opens with an account of a chemist accidentally spilling a reagent and noticing an unexpected color change, then uses that incident throughout the chapter to illustrate principles of chemical indicators.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the opening account in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It provides a memorable, concrete example that anchors abstract concepts discussed later.","It proves that chemical spills are common in laboratories.","It argues against the value of studying chemical indicators.","It states the chapter's main conclusion before any explanation is given."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Using a vivid incident to introduce and later illustrate a technical concept is a common structural device, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-306$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$The op-ed on vertical farming acknowledges that vertical farms use far less land than traditional farms before spending three paragraphs examining whether their high energy costs offset that advantage.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the rhetorical strategy used in the text?$q$, $q$["Addressing a strong point in favor of the opposing view before examining its limitations","Ignoring the land-use advantage entirely to avoid weakening the argument","Presenting only anecdotal evidence without any structured argument","Avoiding any clear thesis so that readers can draw their own conclusions"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Explicitly acknowledging the land-use advantage and then examining its energy costs is a concession-and-complication strategy, described by the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-307$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A profile of an inventor spends its opening paragraph describing a broken kitchen gadget she tinkered with as a child, then details her later career, and closes by returning to a redesigned version of that same gadget, now sold worldwide, without stating the connection directly.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes how the closing paragraph functions in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It creates a deliberate parallel with the opening anecdote, implicitly connecting her early curiosity to her later success.","It introduces a new critique of her business practices.","It shifts the focus entirely away from her inventions to her personal life.","It contradicts the claim made in the opening paragraph."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The closing paragraph revisits the gadget imagery from the opening 'without stating the connection directly,' linking her origin story to her career, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-308$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$An article on tides opens by describing a dramatic high tide that stranded boats on a beach, then explains the gravitational interaction between Earth and the moon that produces tides generally.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It explains the general phenomenon behind the specific event described in the first sentence.","It contradicts the description given in the first sentence.","It introduces a completely unrelated astronomical event.","It proves that tides never strand boats."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence accounts for the stranded boats by explaining the gravitational cause of tides generally, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-309$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay's final paragraph returns to a question about why a weaving pattern survived centuries of change, this time answering it directly after several paragraphs documenting the pattern's uses across generations.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the final paragraph?$q$, $q$["It resolves the question raised at the start of the essay, now supported by the evidence presented.","It introduces a brand-new argument unrelated to the rest of the essay.","It undermines the evidence presented earlier in the essay.","It restates the essay's introduction without adding new information."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The final paragraph directly answers the question from the introduction, now backed by the evidence built up through the essay — a resolving function.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-310$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A science article begins by asserting that deep-sea creatures cannot communicate without sound, then describes the discovery of fish species that flash coordinated light patterns to signal each other, using the finding to overturn the assumption stated at the outset.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the description of the fish in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It provides a counterexample that overturns the assumption presented in the opening sentence.","It confirms the assumption presented in the opening sentence.","It qualifies the opening claim as true only for creatures living below a certain depth.","It summarizes the article's conclusion before any evidence is given."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The passage states directly that the finding is used 'to overturn the assumption stated at the outset' entirely, not to narrow its depth range, making the correct answer the accurate description.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-311$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A museum essay on ceramic glazes opens by describing the glassy sheen visible on a finished bowl, then explains that the sheen results from minerals in the glaze melting and fusing to the clay at specific kiln temperatures.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It reveals the chemical process behind the visual effect described first.","It disputes the claim that the bowl has a glassy sheen.","It argues that the sheen is purely decorative with no chemical basis.","It shifts the essay's focus to an unrelated ceramic tradition."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence explains the chemistry behind the sheen described first, adding explanation rather than disputing or ignoring it.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-312$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$An article opens by describing a single orchid's unusually shaped bloom, then broadens to examine how that shape evolved to attract one specific pollinator species, and finally discusses what the orchid's decline suggests about its pollinator's population.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It moves from a specific example to broader evidence to a wider implication.","It presents two competing theories and evaluates each in turn.","It begins with a general claim and ends with a specific anecdote.","It compares two unrelated flower species throughout the article."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The text follows a clear progression: one orchid, then its evolved relationship with a pollinator, then a broader implication, moving from specific to general.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-313$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay on early railroads spends its first two paragraphs celebrating the speed with which they moved goods across a continent, then devotes its final paragraph to noting how those same railroads displaced communities whose land lay along the new routes.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the final paragraph in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It complicates the earlier celebration by introducing a less positive consequence of the same development.","It repeats the praise offered in the first two paragraphs without adding anything new.","It shifts the topic entirely away from railroads and displaced communities.","It proves that railroads had no effect on the communities involved."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$After celebrating the railroads' speed, the final paragraph introduces a displacing effect of the same development, complicating rather than repeating the earlier praise.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-314$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A history of navigation devotes its opening section to star-based wayfinding used by early seafarers, its middle section to the mechanical sextants of recent centuries, and its final section to the satellite systems that largely replaced both.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It traces the development of a practice chronologically from ancient methods to modern technology.","It presents a single case study and analyzes it from multiple perspectives.","It begins with modern systems and works backward to ancient methods.","It argues that ancient methods were more accurate than modern systems."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The three sections move in chronological order from ancient star-based methods to sextants to satellite systems, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-315$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$An article on bookbinding opens with a description of thread being pulled tight through folded pages, then explains the tension principles that keep a hand-sewn binding from loosening over decades.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It explains the mechanical reasoning behind the technique described in the first sentence.","It contradicts the description given in the first sentence.","It introduces a completely unrelated bookbinding tradition.","It proves that hand-sewn bindings always loosen quickly."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence explains why the thread tension works, accounting for the technique the first sentence describes.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-316$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A report on public libraries opens with a single branch's rising foot traffic after it added free tutoring sessions, then presents citywide circulation data showing similar increases at other branches that added community programming.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the citywide data in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It generalizes a single branch's result into a citywide pattern that strengthens the report's claim.","It contradicts the claim made by the single branch's example.","It defines technical terms related to library administration.","It criticizes branches that did not add new programming."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The citywide data extends the single branch's result to a broader pattern, strengthening rather than contradicting the report's claim.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-317$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay on sign language interpreting acknowledges the common view that interpreting is a simple word-for-word substitution, then spends the remainder of the piece detailing the split-second grammatical restructuring interpreters perform, using this detail to complicate the initial view.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?$q$, $q$["To complicate a simplified view of interpreting with evidence of its real complexity","To argue that interpreting requires no specialized skill","To argue that word-for-word substitution is in fact the most accurate way to interpret","To defend one interpreter against professional criticism"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The essay starts with the word-for-word view, then uses detail about split-second grammatical restructuring to complicate, not confirm, that view, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-318$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A biology chapter opens with a time-lapse description of a tadpole's tail disappearing, then uses that image throughout the chapter to illustrate the broader principle of programmed cell death.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the opening description in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It provides a vivid, concrete image that anchors an abstract biological principle discussed later.","It proves that all amphibians undergo identical metamorphosis.","It argues against studying programmed cell death.","It states the chapter's conclusion before any explanation is given."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Using a vivid image to introduce and later illustrate an abstract principle is a common structural device, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-319$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$An article on furniture restoration opens by describing a chair's wobbling leg, then explains how a loosened glue joint, invisible from the outside, was the actual cause of the wobble.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It identifies the underlying cause of the problem described in the first sentence.","It contradicts the description given in the first sentence.","It introduces an unrelated piece of furniture.","It proves the chair's wobble could not be fixed."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence reveals the hidden cause of the wobble described first, functioning as explanation rather than contradiction.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-320$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$The op-ed on wind energy acknowledges that turbines can disrupt local bird migration before spending the remaining paragraphs describing turbine placement studies that minimize this disruption without reducing power output.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the rhetorical strategy used in the text?$q$, $q$["Conceding a real drawback before showing how it can be mitigated without sacrificing the main benefit","Ignoring the drawback entirely to avoid weakening the argument","Presenting only anecdotal evidence without any structured argument","Avoiding any clear thesis so that readers can draw their own conclusions"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The op-ed concedes the migration drawback, then shows how placement studies mitigate it, a concession-and-mitigation strategy matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-321$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A profile of a composer begins with an extended account of a public failure at her first major premiere, an event she says reshaped how she approached revision. The piece then details her later career, and closes by returning to a triumphant premiere decades later, noting the echo between the two nights without stating it directly.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes how the closing paragraph functions in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It creates a deliberate parallel with the opening anecdote, implicitly connecting early failure to later success.","It introduces a new critique of her later compositions.","It introduces a second composer's triumphant premiere for comparison.","It contradicts the claim made in the opening paragraph."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The closing paragraph revisits her own premiere imagery from the opening 'without stating it directly,' linking her early failure to her later triumph, not introducing a different composer, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-322$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Sleep researcher A found that moderate caffeine intake improved reaction times in sleep-deprived adults.

