  ($q$cs-472$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$Many people believe that goldfish have memories lasting only three seconds. In fact, experiments have shown that goldfish can learn to associate a particular sound with feeding time and remember the association for months. The myth likely persists because it is easy to repeat and because goldfish seem to swim aimlessly.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text?$q$, $q$["It provides a definition of a key term used earlier in the text.","It introduces a new experiment that supports the claim in the first sentence.","It offers a possible explanation for why a mistaken belief endures.","It concludes that goldfish are more intelligent than other fish."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$After the text refutes a myth, the last sentence suggests why the myth persists.$q$, null),
