  ($q$cs-487$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$Imagine a library in which every book is blank except for a single sentence on its spine. This is roughly how early search engines saw the web: they indexed titles and a few keywords rather than the full text of pages. Modern search engines read entire pages, which allows them to answer questions the older systems could not.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text?$q$, $q$["It describes an actual library that was converted into a search engine.","It presents a problem that the text then leaves unsolved.","It offers an analogy that helps readers picture how early search engines worked.","It argues that libraries are obsolete."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The first sentence is a hypothetical image that the second sentence explicitly connects to early search engines.$q$, null),
