  ($q$cs-512$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$Some historians argue that the printing press, by making books cheap, caused the Protestant Reformation. Others counter that the Reformation depended less on technology than on political rivalries among European rulers. Both camps agree, however, that printed pamphlets spread reformers' ideas faster than any earlier medium.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It traces the printing press from its invention to the present.","It presents two competing interpretations of an event and identifies a point on which they agree.","It argues that the printing press had no influence on European history.","It criticizes historians for disagreeing about the Reformation."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Sentence one and two give competing views; sentence three ("Both camps agree") notes common ground.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-513$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$Dozens of languages are spoken in the Caucasus region, many of them found nowhere else. Linguists attribute this diversity to the area's rugged mountains, which kept communities isolated from one another for centuries.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It contrasts the Caucasus with another region.","It questions the accuracy of the claim in the first sentence.","It offers an explanation for the phenomenon described in the first sentence.","It provides a historical timeline of the region's languages."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The second sentence gives the geographic reason for the linguistic diversity noted in the first.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-514$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$In the opening chapter, the author lingers on a deserted train station, noting its broken clocks and peeling posters. This imagery establishes a mood of abandonment that persists through the novel's first half, even as the characters' fortunes begin to change.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It contrasts the train station with a different setting.","It explains the effect of the description mentioned in the first sentence.","It introduces a character who appears later in the novel.","It argues that the opening chapter is the weakest part of the novel."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The second sentence says what the described imagery accomplishes: it sets a lasting mood.$q$, null),
