  ($q$cs-523$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$For decades, biologists assumed that plants respond to their environment only through slow growth. Recent experiments, however, show that some plants can detect the vibrations of a caterpillar's chewing and release defensive chemicals within minutes. These findings suggest that plant responses are faster and more sophisticated than previously believed.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It describes a long-held assumption, presents findings that complicate it, and states a resulting conclusion.","It compares two competing explanations and declares one of them more convincing.","It proposes a hypothesis and then lists several experiments that failed to support it.","It narrates a single researcher's career from early experiments to later recognition."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The first sentence gives an old assumption, the second gives new evidence ("however") that complicates it, and the third states what the findings suggest.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-524$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$The octopus's arms contain more neurons than its central brain, which allows each arm to explore and react independently. A severed arm, for instance, will continue to grasp at objects for some time. This distributed arrangement helps explain how an octopus can manipulate several objects at once.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It summarizes the argument of the entire text.","It raises an objection to the claim made in the first sentence.","It defines the term \"neurons.\"","It gives a specific example of the independence of the octopus's arms described in the first sentence."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$"For instance" signals that the second sentence offers an example of the arms' independence.$q$, null),
