  ($q$cs-585$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$A scientist's essay begins with the question 'Why do we yawn?' It then reviews three leading explanations and concludes that none has been conclusively proven.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the opening question?$q$, $q$["It undermines the credibility of the scientist.","It introduces an unrelated anecdote.","It states the essay's final conclusion.","It frames the topic the essay will explore."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The question introduces the puzzle that the essay then examines.$q$, null),
