  ($q$cs-587$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$An essay about urban beekeeping opens with a vivid description of rooftop hives at sunrise, then shifts to data on declining wild bee populations.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the effect of the shift from description to data?$q$, $q$["It undercuts the importance of urban beekeeping.","It places a personal scene in the context of a larger ecological concern.","It changes the topic to rooftop architecture.","It replaces the author's argument with a counterargument."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The data frame the vivid scene as part of a broader concern about bees.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-588$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$The author of a profile of a retired teacher opens with a former student's anecdote about the teacher's unconventional grading, and then offers her own observation that the teacher's methods, though odd, produced unusually engaged students.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the author's own observation?$q$, $q$["It evaluates the teacher's methods in light of the anecdote.","It summarizes the teacher's retirement plans.","It disputes the student's account.","It introduces a rival teaching philosophy."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The author's observation assesses the methods that the anecdote illustrated.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-589$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A literary critic first summarizes a widely held view that a novel's ending is bleak. She then argues that the final image of a lit window actually suggests hope, and that readers have overlooked it.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the critic's argument?$q$, $q$["She describes the novel's plot in chronological order.","She raises a question and leaves it unanswered.","She introduces a theory and then applies it to several novels.","She presents a common interpretation and then offers a competing one."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$She sets out the prevailing view, then argues for a different reading.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-590$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$In a history of a canal, the author explains that early critics called the project wasteful. The author then notes that within a decade the canal carried more cargo than any road in the region.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the role of the second sentence?$q$, $q$["It confirms the critics' prediction.","It describes the canal's construction methods.","It introduces a new topic unrelated to the canal.","It presents evidence that complicates the critics' early assessment."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The cargo data undercut the critics' claim that the canal was wasteful.$q$, null),
