  ($q$cs-593$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$The author argues that public libraries remain essential. She first acknowledges that books are now easily available online, then argues that libraries provide services such as computer access and community programs that the internet cannot replace.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence about online books?$q$, $q$["It acknowledges a possible objection before the author responds to it.","It states the author's main claim.","It introduces a personal anecdote.","It provides statistics about book sales."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The author concedes a point in order to rebut it.$q$, null),
