  ($q$cs-624$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$A passage describes a bakery's busy morning rush and ends with a single sentence: 'By ten, the shelves were bare and the baker finally sat down.'$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the last sentence?$q$, $q$["It compares the bakery with a rival.","It introduces a new character.","It marks the end of the rush and shows its effect on the baker.","It defines the word 'rush.'"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The sentence concludes the scene by showing the result of the busy morning.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-625$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$The author begins with a brief story about getting lost on a hike. She then explains three basic navigation skills every hiker should learn.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the opening story?$q$, $q$["It argues against hiking.","It lists the three navigation skills.","It provides a map of the trail.","It introduces the topic by showing why the skills matter."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The anecdote motivates the skills the author goes on to explain.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-626$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$A scientist writes: 'Most people picture the deep ocean as empty. In fact, it teems with life that produces its own light.'$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence?$q$, $q$["It corrects a common misconception stated in the first.","It provides a definition of 'deep ocean.'","It repeats the first sentence in different words.","It introduces an unrelated topic."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence counters the belief described in the first.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-627$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$The author of an essay on typewriters notes that they have become popular again among young writers, and then suggests that the appeal lies in the absence of distractions such as notifications.$q$, $q$Which choice best states the main purpose of the second part of the text?$q$, $q$["To compare typewriters to modern printers.","To describe how typewriters work.","To offer an explanation for a trend described earlier.","To argue that typewriters should be banned."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The suggestion explains why typewriters are popular again.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-628$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$A passage describes a lighthouse keeper's solitary routine in precise, unemotional detail. The final line reads: 'He had not spoken aloud in eleven days.'$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the effect of the final line?$q$, $q$["It highlights the keeper's isolation through a stark fact.","It reveals the lighthouse's location.","It introduces a dispute with another character.","It shows the keeper enjoying his routine."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The blunt detail underscores how isolated the keeper is.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-629$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A biologist begins by describing a puzzling observation: a certain frog species is thriving in a polluted pond. She then proposes two possible explanations and describes an experiment to test them.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It presents a puzzle, proposes explanations, and outlines a way to test them.","It contrasts two unrelated species.","It argues for a single conclusion without evidence.","It traces a historical timeline."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The text moves from observation to hypotheses to a test.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-630$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$In the first paragraph, a critic summarizes the plot of a controversial film. In the second, she argues that the film's critics have confused the characters' views with the filmmaker's own.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second paragraph?$q$, $q$["It criticizes the film's acting.","It summarizes the film's ending.","It compares the film with a novel.","It defends the film against a particular misreading."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The second paragraph argues that critics have misread the film.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-631$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A chapter on the history of refrigeration first explains how households once relied on ice delivered by horse-drawn wagons. It then argues that electric refrigerators, by removing that dependence, changed not only diets but also the layout of cities.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence?$q$, $q$["It defines the term 'refrigerator.'","It rejects the idea that diets changed.","It establishes the earlier practice that the later development replaced.","It argues that ice delivery should return."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The first sentence sets up the baseline the author then contrasts with electric refrigeration.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-632$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$The author notes that critics have praised the memoir for its honesty. She then observes that the memoir omits entire years of the author's life, and suggests that its candor is therefore selective.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence?$q$, $q$["It complicates the praise described in the first sentence.","It summarizes the memoir's plot.","It introduces an unrelated memoir.","It repeats the critics' praise."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The omission complicates the claim that the memoir is fully honest.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-633$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$In an essay about maps, the author begins: 'Every map lies.' She goes on to explain that flattening a sphere onto paper necessarily distorts either shape or area.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the opening statement?$q$, $q$["It offers a provocative claim that the rest of the text explains.","It asks readers to draw their own map.","It states a fact that the author later denies.","It describes a specific map in detail."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The bold statement is clarified by the explanation of map distortion.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-634$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$A text describes how a village celebrates the first snowfall each year with a communal meal. It concludes that the tradition helps neighbors feel connected.$q$, $q$Which choice best states the main idea of the text?$q$, $q$["A seasonal tradition helps strengthen a sense of community.","Meals should be shared only in winter.","Snow is rare in the region.","The village is cold all year."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The text focuses on the tradition's connecting effect.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-635$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A scientist describes an experiment in which plants exposed to classical music grew slightly taller than those in silence. She cautions that the difference was small and may not be meaningful.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the scientist's caution?$q$, $q$["It rejects the experiment's design entirely.","It tempers the significance of the experiment's result.","It confirms that music causes plants to grow.","It introduces a new experiment."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The caution limits how much to read into the small difference.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-636$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$The author contrasts the quiet of a library in the morning with its bustle after school. She writes that the same room 'seems to hold two different lives.'$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence?$q$, $q$["It describes the library's collection.","It argues for longer library hours.","It introduces a new topic.","It sums up the contrast with a figurative image."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The figurative statement encapsulates the contrast the author drew.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-637$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$A scholar argues that early photographs of Native communities, though often treated as neutral records, reflected the photographers' choices about what to include and what to omit.$q$, $q$Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?$q$, $q$["To describe the technology used in early cameras.","To catalog the communities depicted.","To challenge the assumption that the photographs are neutral documents.","To argue that photographs should be destroyed."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The scholar questions the neutrality of the photographs.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-638$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$The author of a book review opens by quoting a famous line from the book, then argues that the line, often cited as the book's thesis, is actually contradicted by the book's later chapters.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the opening quotation?$q$, $q$["It introduces a commonly cited idea that the review then challenges.","It provides biographical details about the author.","It illustrates a point about grammar.","It summarizes the review's main conclusion."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The quotation sets up the popular reading the reviewer disputes.$q$, null),
