  ($q$cs-659$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$In 1928, scientist Alexander Fleming noticed that mold growing in one of his dishes had killed the bacteria around it. That accidental discovery led to penicillin, one of the first antibiotics.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?$q$, $q$["To describe how an important medicine was discovered by accident","To argue that most important scientific discoveries happen by accident","To explain how mold grows in laboratory dishes over several days","To list the many ways that antibiotics are used by doctors today"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The text tells how Fleming's chance observation led to penicillin. It doesn't claim that all discoveries are accidents.$q$, null),
